[E0356] Error: this loop stands for a value, and yields none
   ╭─[ err/199_generators/main.wip:8:16 ]
   │
 8 │     var none = for x in xs { val y = x }
   │                ────────────┬────────────
   │                            ╰────────────── no `yield` in it
   │
   │ Help: hand each value over with `yield`, or write the loop as a statement
   │
   │ Note: a loop where a value stands is a generator, whose values are what it yields
───╯
[E0357] Error: cannot `return` from a loop that is a generator
    ╭─[ err/199_generators/main.wip:14:13 ]
    │
 12 │ ╭─▶     var early = for x in xs {
    ┆ ┆
 14 │ │               return
    │ │               ───┬──
    │ │                  ╰──── the loop runs as its values are asked for
    ┆ ┆
 17 │ ├─▶     }
    │ │
    │ ╰─────────── a generator
    │
    │     Help: end the loop with `break`
    │
    │     Note: the loop runs later, from whoever asks for its values, so there is no function around it to leave; `break` ends it
────╯
[E0356] Error: `silent` answers an `Iterator`, and yields nothing
    ╭─[ err/199_generators/main.wip:20:4 ]
    │
 20 │ fn silent(n: i64): Iterator<i64> = {
    │    ───┬──          ──────┬──────
    │       ╰─────────────────────────── no `yield` in its body
    │                          │
    │                          ╰──────── a generator
    │
    │ Help: hand each value over with `yield`
    │
    │ Note: a function that answers `Iterator<T>` is a generator, whose values are what its body yields
