[E0358] Error: a function that yields cannot take `v`, a `&var`
    ╭─[ err/199_generators/main.wip:24:10 ]
    │
 24 │ fn grows(v: &var Vec<i64>): Iterator<i64> = {
    │          ────────┬───────
    │                  ╰───────── the generator would hold it between calls
    │
    │ Help: take it as `&`, or collect the values with `own for`, which runs while the call does
    │
    │ Note: a function that yields answers a generator, which keeps what it was given until its values are asked for; it may read what it borrows, but not change it
────╯
[E0359] Error: `leaves` would hold itself, and be endlessly large
    ╭─[ err/199_generators/main.wip:38:30 ]
    │
 38 │                 for value in leaves(&child) {
    │                              ───────┬──────
    │                                     ╰──────── a generator held here, by value, that holds this one
    │
    │ Help: put the inner one on the heap
    │
    │ Note: a generator keeps what it walks inside itself, so one that walks itself holds itself; on the heap, it holds a pointer
